4.5 Financial Analysis
The financial analysis assessed the profitability of the poultry enterprise by comparing production costs with income generated.
Major Expenditure Items
•	Purchase of chicks.
•	Construction materials.
•	Feed.
•	Vaccines and drugs.
•	Equipment.
•	Litter materials.
•	Miscellaneous expenses.
Sources of Income
•	Sale of mature birds.
•	Sale of poultry manure .
4.6 Cost–Benefit Analysis
Total Income – Total Expenditure
KSHs (215,000 – 160,000) = Kshs 55,000 
The enterprise demonstrated the potential to generate income while providing practical agricultural training.
Benefits realized included:
•	Income from sale of birds.
•	Practical learning experience.
•	Improved entrepreneurship skills.
•	Production of organic manure.
•	Demonstration of climate-smart livestock farming.
Although feed constituted the largest production cost, efficient management and proper marketing contributed to the enterprise's viability.
